// cppcheck cannot see a lambda's side effect on a captured variable, so it reads
// `have_pending` as unchanged across sealAggregate() and calls the follow-up
// test redundant. It is not: sealAggregate sets it.
identicalInnerCondition:src/daemon/modes/BridgeMode.cpp
// The queue size is changed by another thread under the same lock while this
// waits on a condition variable; cppcheck models neither, so it reads the guard
// as constant.
knownConditionTrueFalse:src/core/phy/SoftwarePhy.cpp
// stop() is called from each mode's OWN destructor, where the object is still
// that type. Non-virtual dispatch is correct here, not a bug.
virtualCallInConstructor
